1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,960
Medical card, admission paperwork. Now that we have your ID and receipt, we should be good to head home.

2
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,240
Hey, thanks again for this, Dad.

3
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:22,840
I'm not your father.

4
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:30,060
At least those kids should be safe for right now. Must be bad if they're having to hide Lu Guang.

5
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:35,500
I know. From what we saw of his wounds, they must be mixed up in something dangerous.

6
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:41,760
Good thing Dad can pass for Lu Guang. It gave him a reason to shave and get a haircut. Doesn't he look good?

7
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,220
He most certainly does. I'm a little jealous now.

8
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:49,260
Hey, you. This place is a hospital, not a morgue. So go die somewhere else.

9
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:58,180
You're hogging my seat. Huh? What are you, deaf? Hey, do you understand words, you old fart? Get lost.

10
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:05,540
Ah, why are you even here? I thought geezers like you all had bedtimes. You're too old to live the nightlife.

11
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,780
Hey, you didn't answer me.

12
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:12,600
All right, that's enough. Show some respect for your elders. Don't let him get to you, Dad.

13
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,760
Don't call me old. Or your dad.

14
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:16,420
Would you please, Cutter?

15
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:18,020
Come on. We're leaving anyway.

16
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:22,520
Yeah, you better leave. Stupid old people being here late at night.

17
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:30,640
Somebody help. Call the doctor. I was out having fun and now my stomach hurts real bad.

18
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:35,960
Come on, just make it stop already. It's killing me.

19
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:38,620
Ah! Holy hell, is that a snake?

20
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:51,620
That grown man has it coming.

21
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,220
Dad, would you please let it go now?

22
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,680
Wait, I almost forgot. Sorry.

23
00:01:56,680 --> 00:02:01,300
I wanted to check in with Xiaoling before we left. I'll only be a moment.

24
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,380
That's odd. She's not answering her phone.

25
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:14,520
What? Do you think something happened to her?

26
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:19,740
She could be fine, but I'm getting a bad feeling. There might be trouble.

27
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:22,500
Should we go back to the ward and check on them?

28
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,480
Hmm. It looks like it's too late for that.

29
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:29,080
You see those men walking towards the building behind us?

30
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,780
They're practically reeking with murderous intent.

31
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,920
You're right. We have to hurry.

32
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:37,620
Hold on. I want to help them out as much as you do.

33
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,900
But remember what Xiaoling said. We can't let them see us.

34
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:44,060
But they need our help. There has to be a way.

35
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,940
Sorry we took Xiaoling. We had to pick up something on the way over.

36
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,840
I can't believe this is real.

37
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,920
What do you say they were? Triple what?

38
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,540
Xiaoling warriors!

39
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,580
More like the triple star geezers.

40
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:11,700
Go on. Do the thing.

41
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,920
Say, door of courage. Sweeping away the fear with a lightness.

42
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,500
I'm sorry.

43
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,260
You two in the back should leave.

44
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,740
We've got this.

45
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,180
Yeah. Sure.

46
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:25,320
Hey.

47
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,040
You sound like you're a bit too old to be playing hero.

48
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,580
So what? Is this supposed to be like a senior citizens club or something?

49
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,080
Isn't it late for you?

50
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,240
Why don't you go on home and get some rest?

51
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:51,460
You're trying not to get people killed, remember?

52
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,360
What kind of freak are you?

53
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,580
You nearly took his head off.

54
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,600
No, you probably don't want to, but you're going to need to hold back on them.

55
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,440
He's right, Dad.

56
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:01,780
They're nothing but three old loons wearing costumes.

57
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,300
Take them out!

58
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:11,300
We've tolerated your evil wrong enough!

59
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,800
For a beautiful world, we will stop you!

60
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:28,240
Cut the act.

61
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,400
Tell us what happened at the hospital.

62
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,960
I'm very sorry, sir.

63
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,500
But I've told you everything I can remember.

64
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,020
You haven't said anything!

65
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,480
Now quit giving us the runaround.

66
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:40,840
Tell me!

67
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,900
But it's true!

68
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,660
All I remember was a flash of white light.

69
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,680
Then I woke up and my whole body was screaming in pain.

70
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,920
I saw a light and then I was on the ground.

71
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:52,540
I'm pretty sure I was dead for a little bit.

72
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,420
Yeah, I saw the light.

73
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,140
It was something else, man.

74
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,480
I felt light enough to float up into the sky.

75
00:04:58,740 --> 00:04:59,480
It's a paradise.

76
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,860
It was one of those out-of-body experiences.

77
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:05,140
And this happened because you were beaten half to death by a superhero?

78
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:05,980
Come on!

79
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:06,340
Yeah.

80
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:07,300
No.

81
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,920
Not just one guy.

82
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,000
It was the Triple Star Warriors.

83
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,420
They tore through us like we were nothing!

84
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,960
Well, this is going nowhere.

85
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,140
I guess they're tougher than we thought.

86
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:22,620
I'm telling you, it was like watching a pissed-off martial god just unload their wrath.

87
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
I'm glad you're okay.

88
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,060
Well, we had help.

89
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:25,760
We're fine.

90
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:26,900
How about you?

91
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:27,660
Feel safe?

92
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:29,240
Security's much better.

93
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:31,740
The police are patrolling all the time now.

94
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,960
At least three officers are watching me at all times.

95
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:37,200
They rotate sometimes, just to be safe.

96
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,260
Now it's a lot harder for the killer to take over anyone who's on guard duty.

97
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:46,940
I think Captain Xiao wanted to make sure that if someone gets possessed, the others can stop him.

98
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:50,720
A lot has happened in the past few days.

99
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:51,780
I'm exhausted.

100
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,180
I need a nap.

101
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:53,980
Rest.

102
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:56,100
But make sure your door's locked first.

103
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:58,140
You can't be too cautious right now.

104
00:05:59,400 --> 00:05:59,880
Wait.

105
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,260
What if you end up getting possessed?

106
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,260
Then he'll be all along with the killer.

107
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:06,080
You better handcuff yourself to the bed.

108
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,120
Is it me or did Lu Guang seem off?

109
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:23,240
Well, after everything he's been through, I would be more worried if he acted normally.

110
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:24,700
You're right.

111
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:26,200
Guess we're all still on edge.

112
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:28,840
Captain?

113
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,480
What happened to you?

114
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,620
I was attacked outside of the hospital.

115
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:35,660
They caught me off guard.

116
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:37,260
What about Officer Chen?

117
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:42,500
Do you have any idea who it was that attacked you?

118
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:44,980
Was it the people who attacked Officer Chen?

119
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,540
Did they take Liu Min's phone?

120
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,780
I don't have answers.

121
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,360
I screwed up.

122
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,640
And now we're stuck.

123
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,040
All of this happened because of my plan.

124
00:06:53,040 --> 00:07:06,220
No, Captain.

125
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,800
You were keeping us safe the best you could.

126
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,220
We're grateful for that.

127
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:10,900
Yeah.

128
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,740
And thanks for keeping our powers a secret.

129
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,760
I'll ask for a demotion.

130
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,580
I got my partner killed.

131
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:17,560
That's on me.

132
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:21,820
But for right now, I have a murderer to catch.

133
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:23,520
Let us help.

134
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:27,140
Officer Chen, Emma, and who knows how many others.

135
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,500
We can't let their deaths be in vain.

136
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:32,320
I've already said as much to the higher-ups.

137
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,480
Not sure what they'll say.

138
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,660
This is all highly unprecedented.

139
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:39,240
But that can wait.

140
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:40,900
First, we need answers.

141
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,760
And we know one man who might have them.

142
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:48,200
Where did you learn to interrogate like that?

143
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,840
Guess old pigs can learn new tricks.

144
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,080
Enough.

145
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:57,620
Captain, this one's a talker, all right.

146
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:58,780
Just nothing useful.

147
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:01,500
Did you push Officer Chen off the roof?

148
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:02,720
Who, me?

149
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,060
You think I pushed that well-trained policeman?

150
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:07,820
How flattered do you think I could do anything to him?

151
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,560
If you ask me, he did it himself.

152
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:14,020
Why would you assume suicide?

153
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:14,980
Huh?

154
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,600
We know you were on the roof.

155
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:22,740
Well, I was going up onto the roof to get some fresh air.

156
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:23,780
Then I heard it.

157
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:26,720
Sounded like a sissy was ugly crying about something.

158
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,560
They kept saying, I'm sorry, over and over.

159
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:33,560
I rushed to see if I could help, but I got there right as they jumped down.

160
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:35,600
I was so scared, I ran inside.

161
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:37,040
Such a tragedy.

162
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:39,760
What could possess him to do that?

163
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:43,600
Maybe he felt bad for taking something he shouldn't.

164
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:44,380
Enough!

165
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:45,660
You take that back!

166
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,680
Calm down, Detective.

167
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,240
Stress kills, you know.

168
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,720
I was just guessing.

169
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,060
But that anger?

170
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,520
It's almost like you've got something to hide.

171
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,040
Chen Bean was a good man.

172
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,460
No one's going to believe he was corrupt.

173
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:01,900
Really?

174
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:05,020
He probably shouldn't have taken all those bribes then.

175
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,860
Not the best career move.

176
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,140
Check his kitchen if you don't believe me.

177
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:24,600
Say one more word about him and you're dead!

178
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,100
Captain, it's not worth it for me!

179
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,100
You won't get away with this, asshole!

180
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,380
I'll prove he's innocent!

181
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:40,020
Yes, yes, I'm aware of that.

182
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:43,500
His death is connected to Liu Min's suicide.

183
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,220
Chen Bean's innocent.

184
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,900
Once I prove it, you'll know why the money was there.

185
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:53,760
Those two are special, but they need time, of course, I'm sure.

186
00:09:53,760 --> 00:10:01,920
Yes, I understand.

187
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,020
It's not clear to me, either.

188
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,560
I'll update you if anything changes.

189
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:12,420
I appreciate all your support with this.

190
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,220
The higher-ups are holding off till the case is closed.

191
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,180
They suspended the stabbing case.

192
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:20,920
That's good.

193
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:25,260
So, um, Liu Guang asked me to bring this.

194
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:28,320
He wanted to be here, but there was an unexpected snack.

195
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,060
I swear I'll come right back.

196
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,060
It'll be fine.

197
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:32,120
Please.

198
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:33,180
Not on your life!

199
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:35,960
I'm not letting you traipse off so you can reopen your wound!

200
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,400
Now get back in bed!

201
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,040
You want your guts to fall out?

202
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:44,580
Um, on second thought, I should get back in bed.

203
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:48,000
Liu Guang needs to rest for now.

204
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:49,060
But you're here.

205
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,020
That's enough.

206
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,700
Mr. Xiao, what's next?

207
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:53,700
Is there a plan?

208
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:54,500
Huh.

209
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,800
What a coincidence.

210
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,980
My son's memorial is right next to your partner's.

211
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:02,020
Are you here to mourn or finally give us some answers as to what happened?

212
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:07,280
Our son died in your interrogation room, and you think that I'm going to buy some bull about him strangling himself?

213
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,120
How stupid do you think I am?

214
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,780
My son wasn't depressed or mentally ill in any way.

215
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,740
Maybe you can tell me why he's dead.

216
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:14,780
I'm sorry.

217
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:17,140
He was related to multiple cases.

218
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,460
None of which are closed yet.

219
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:19,740
Oh, really?

220
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,520
Tell me about them.

221
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,880
Better yet, tell me why you killed him.

222
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,200
Please calm down.

223
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,240
Again, I'm sorry.

224
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,480
But he's gone.

225
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:29,680
Blaming the police won't change that.

226
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:34,240
You should know we caught your son breaking into their studio.

227
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,560
Yeah, that's true.

228
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:36,560
He was there too.

229
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:37,380
I don't care!

230
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,400
You can't prove it, and the dead can't deny.

231
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,460
Mr. Chen, didn't you say we could sue?

232
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,400
Yes.

233
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,320
Say the word.

234
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:46,880
Really?

235
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:49,180
When did you sell your soul, huh?

236
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:51,600
I still remember the cop you used to be.

237
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:53,040
So what happened?

238
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:58,920
Justice needs proof, not assumptions.

239
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:02,860
Don't do it!

240
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:05,380
We're police officers, not vigilantes!

241
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,880
You don't have to help me.

242
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,680
Just don't stop me from bringing that bastard to justice.

243
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:15,300
Huh.

244
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,520
You hear that?

245
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:20,340
If you can't find proof against my son, my lawyer will destroy you!

246
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,720
Cases take time.

247
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,200
I'm not waiting any longer.

248
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,880
With every delay, you spit on my son's grave!

249
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,860
I saw him attack someone with a knife.

250
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:28,580
I'll testify.

251
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,320
Oh, you will?

252
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:32,780
That's nonsense if I've ever heard it.

253
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:35,720
Liu Min was disabled.

254
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:38,100
He could barely move or do anything.

255
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:40,400
And you saw him attack someone?

256
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,000
That's just insane.

257
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,700
Mr. Chen, if they fake the evidence,

258
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,960
could we get more money out of it?

259
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:48,520
Why, yes, of course.

260
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:49,340
A lot more.

261
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,260
And they'd face charges.

262
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:56,100
Sounds like you better be careful.

263
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,600
Life must be so hard on a fixed salary.

264
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,500
Enough for a young officer to start taking bribes.

265
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:04,000
Shut up!

266
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,540
There's hardly room for baseless accusations!

267
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:09,100
But you can frame our child.

268
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:11,640
I was only talking about what I'd heard.

269
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,100
What's more, it's not baseless.

270
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,620
The secret is out.

271
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,420
The cops found the money that he hid.

272
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,700
Not another word!

273
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:21,440
You can't stop me.

274
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,960
I'll scream from the rooftops if I so choose.

275
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:24,400
What?

276
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,440
You want to fight?

277
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:26,200
Fine.

278
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,760
Go on and hit me, you prick!

279
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:42,340
Oh god, you all saw that, right?

280
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,160
He attacked first!

281
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,960
You're a policeman, so arrest that man!

282
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,220
He was literally asking for it, though.

283
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:50,180
You worthless rat!

284
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:51,640
Where do you get off?

285
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:54,720
Did your folks abandon you before they taught you respect?

286
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,380
Xin Xin!

287
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,260
Let him go!

288
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,100
Not yet.

289
00:13:57,460 --> 00:13:58,780
Apologize.

290
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,080
Apologize for what?

291
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:11,100
The only attack I saw is on your face.

292
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:12,780
Way to go, landlady.

293
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:13,640
Hell yeah.

294
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,240
You're a landlady?

295
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:19,020
I want that violent maniac arrested right now!

296
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:20,380
You good?

297
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,660
Xin Xin, it's your call.

298
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:25,100
I can handcuff her if you want.

299
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:28,040
Let's meet up at the station.

300
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:29,420
Get your statement.

301
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:32,160
For this scratch, no.

302
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,960
You can't just walk away!

303
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:37,840
Enough!

304
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,040
Don't embarrass me.

305
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,800
Just let it go, okay?

306
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:43,140
Let's leave before you make things worse.

307
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:57,380
When did you take this?

308
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,340
It looks recent.

309
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:01,260
Oh, it's from when we got married.

310
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:03,140
What?

311
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:05,520
Uh, nothing.

312
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:08,420
Time sure flies.

313
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:13,340
I took that two years ago, and we still haven't had our ceremony.

314
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,000
Shouldn't Officer Chen's wife be here by now?

315
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,600
She should, but I couldn't find her.

316
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,680
Where is she?

317
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:29,740
It's getting late.

318
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,240
I'm worried.

319
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,480
What if something happened?

320
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:37,780
Uh, have I heard this before?

321
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:41,480
Look, she's here!

322
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:41,840
Huh?

323
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,260
Where are you going?

324
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,040
Let's go, huh?

325
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,360
I didn't know.

326
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:43,720
No, it's not.

327
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:45,840
Come on, what are you gonna do?

328
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:46,180
They're real.

329
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:46,740
Get in.

330
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:50,740
Let's not tell her.

331
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:51,580
Just let her open.

332
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:52,500
This is very.

333
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,880
This is again the folks!

334
00:15:54,880 --> 00:16:23,520
You inconsiderate bastard, you lying selfish jerk!

335
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:28,520
Damn you! Look at you abandon me!

336
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:29,520
Over here!

337
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:33,520
You finally have some time off and you want to spend it here?

338
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:36,520
Why not? We can stay home when we get old.

339
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:41,520
And why? Why did you have to break every promise that you ever made me?

340
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:46,520
You said you would stay with me when we went shopping.

341
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:51,520
Or sit through a movie together from beginning time.

342
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:58,520
So many nights alone. You'd tell me you would come home soon, but you never did.

343
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,520
Hey, I assume you're still working?

344
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,520
Yeah, sorry. I'm almost done though.

345
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:13,520
I'm still waiting. Why haven't you come home yet?

346
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:18,520
Please don't force our daughter to grow up without ever having a chance to meet her father.

347
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:21,520
It just doesn't fit her. You know that.

348
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:24,520
It's too late for you to make up for the past.

349
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,520
But there's one last promise that I need from you.

350
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,520
You owe me.

351
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:34,520
Promise that you'll pay me back in our next life.

352
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,520
Okay?

353
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,520
It's done, my lady.

354
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:38,520
It's done, my lady.

355
00:17:38,520 --> 00:18:05,520
What?

356
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:08,800
How was it?

357
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,420
You all right?

358
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,820
There's been so much pain.

359
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:16,660
They didn't deserve this.

360
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,580
So, we should help them.

361
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:33,200
Yeah, we should.

362
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:41,980
Hey, stay right there.

363
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,780
Okay, sure thing.

364
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,700
What is this for?

365
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:05,040
I, Chenbin, am proposing to the love of my life.

366
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,620
In this moment, and every one after.

367
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:11,640
I'm sorry I can't always be there for the small things.

368
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:14,080
But I'm always leaving you alone.

369
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:18,080
Whether it's when we're shopping, or halfway through watching a movie.

370
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:24,540
And thank you for forgiving me, even during the times that I don't deserve it.

371
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:30,640
I swear, with all my heart, to love and protect you,

372
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:35,220
not just for the rest of this life, but the next and the next.

373
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:40,060
So, will you marry me?

374
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:45,980
Well, duh.

375
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:47,540
I already said yes, right?

376
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:51,960
But one proposal doesn't guarantee I'll say yes in my next life.

377
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:53,400
It's not that easy.

378
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:59,520
Then again, if you keep making me fall in love with you, I'll have to.

379
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:19,720
Wait!

380
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:24,200
Please!

